{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLClef","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Sometimes clefs are added to the staff in non-standard line positions, either to indicate cue passages, or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"when there are multiple clefs present simultaneously on one staff. In this situation, the additional attribute","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is set to “yes” and the line value is ignored. The size attribute is used for clefs where the additional","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attribute is “yes”. It is typically used to indicate cue clefs.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Sometimes clefs at the start of a measure need to appear after the barline rather than before, as for cues or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for use after a repeated section. The after-barline attribute is set to “yes” in this situation. The attribute","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is ignored for mid-measure clefs.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Clefs appear at the start of each system unless the print-object attribute has been set to “no” or the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"additional attribute has been set to “yes”.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps the MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<clef>"},{"text":" element.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLClef","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"text":"Clefs are represented by a combination of sign, line, and clef-octave-change elements. The o